{:adr-id "2607152100"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-0510 — Hard Coal Mining Operations Coordination (verified redo)"
 :date "2026-07-14"
 :author "Cloud Itonami Contributors"
 :status :accepted
 :context
 "ISIC Rev.4 0510 (Mining of hard coal) had an earlier same-day scaffold
  promoted to :implemented on the promoting agent's own claim of 'all
  tests green'; an independent audit re-ran clojure -M:test directly
  and found 16 tests / 10 failures, reverted to :spec. Root cause:
  mining.store MemStore test fixtures keyed the site directory with
  keyword site-ids while every lookup used the string :site-id off the
  proposal, so every site lookup silently returned nil and every
  proposal (including intended-clean happy paths) was misclassified as
  a HARD site-unregistered hold. This ADR documents a from-scratch,
  independently re-verified redo, renamed mining.* -> coalops.*,
  mirroring cloud-itonami-isic-0891's module shape and
  cloud-itonami-isic-0710's coordination-only scope boundary."
 :decision
 {:scope-boundary
  "Coordination-only actor. Closed four-op allowlist, all :effect
   :propose: log-production-record, schedule-maintenance,
   flag-safety-concern (always escalates), coordinate-shipment. An op
   outside this set is the same failure mode as forbidden-scope
   content, not a separate carve-out."
  :governor-rules
  "Three HARD, permanent, un-overridable checks: (1) site-unverified --
   target site must be independently :registered?/:verified? in the
   store, never trusted from the proposal's own claim; (2)
   effect-not-propose -- any :effect other than :propose is a claim to
   directly actuate outside governance; (3) scope-exclusion -- any
   proposal (any op) touching blasting/drilling-pattern/cutting-
   schedule/extraction-sequencing/ventilation-control/gas-monitoring-
   override/mine-safety-authority territory, evaluated unconditionally
   via a lower-cased EN+JA substring scan of the proposal's own
   content. Escalation (soft): flag-safety-concern always, low
   confidence (<0.6). coalops.phase independently agrees --
   flag-safety-concern never auto-commits at any phase."
  :root-cause-fix
  "String-vs-keyword map-key mismatch in the prior mining.store test
   fixtures silently defeated every site lookup. coalops.store keys the
   site directory consistently on the string :site-id everywhere,
   verified by coalops.store-contract-test."
  :module-shape
  "Renamed mining.* -> coalops.*: store (MemStore), advisor
   (CoalOpsAdvisor, mock + real-LLM seam via langchain.model, plus an
   :out-of-scope? test hook), governor (CoalMiningGovernor), phase
   (0->3 rollout), operation (langgraph-clj StateGraph), sim (demo
   driver)."}
 :consequences
 ["Registry entry corrected in place (exact-text edit of the existing"
  " {:id \"0510\" ...} block): REVERTED comment removed, :maturity :implemented"
  "Actor repo cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-0510 rewritten and pushed to main"
  "Test suite run directly by this session: Ran 43 tests containing 133"
  " assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors (both at push time and again from a"
  " fresh post-merge clone). clj-kondo: 0 errors, 0 warnings."
  "Checked-in example of the string-vs-keyword map-key-mismatch bug class"
  " for future actor builds in this fleet to grep their own store"
  " contract tests for"]
 :references
 ["cloud-itonami-isic-0891/src/chemmineops/ (module-shape mirror)"
  "cloud-itonami-isic-0710/docs/adr/ (coordination-only scope-boundary precedent)"
  "kotoba-lang/industry resources/kotoba/industry/registry.edn \"0510\" entry"
